WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.130
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, I finally had
a chance to watch Amazing Spider-Man 2 so

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:09.480
I wanted to do a review and talk about the
Sinister Six spinoff movies and the direct

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.480
Spider-Man sequels they’ve announced.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.249
If you didn’t hear last year, they’re
basically creating their own Spider Move-Verse

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:17.830
at Sony just like Marvel has done.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.130
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do regular movie reviews for my favorite

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.090
sci fi, fantasy and comic book movies.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.600
I even have a dedicated day for Marvel videos
on Tuesdays.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.920
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.160
And let’s a dream of the day Marvel gets
the rights back to Spider-Man, so he can take

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.590
his rightful place in the Avengers.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.060
Along with Wolverine.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.980
So since there’s so much to talk about this
is how I’m going to do it.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.210
I’ll do my review first, then talk about
the Sinister Six and the the post credits

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.210
scene.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.630
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.920
Let’s start with what I loved the most about
the movie.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:52.920
The actors.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.829
Yes Andrew Garfield and Emma Stone are the
leads but I want to give some special attention

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:59.050
to Jamie Foxx and Dane Dehaan.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.760
There was actually something funny I saw on
twitter.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.700
A lot of the film critics I know were calling
the movie the best Batman Forever reboot ever.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:13.080
They compared Jamie Foxx’s Electro to The
Riddler and Dane Dehaan to Tommy Lee Jones

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.080
emo Two-Face.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.080
It’s not meant to make fun of them.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.310
It’s just a funny meta way to think about
their performances.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.520
He really is one of the best comedic character
actors out there.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.490
The reason he was in Django Unchained was
because Will Smith didn’t want to play a

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.490
slave.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.479
Jamie Foxx on the other hand is fearless when
it comes to putting himself into characters.

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:35.760
He’s not typecast like other A-List actors,
so he gets to have a lot more fun.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.260
A la Electro and Sinister Six next.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:49.320
Everytime I see a big movie like this I try
to figure out which scene they read in the

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.010
audition.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:56.940
And I felt like Jamie Foxx did that Birthday
Cake scene in his apartment.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.940
That’s the scene where you learn everything
you need to know about his character.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.331
His ticks, the way he perceives himself and
the way he thinks about everyone else.

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:04.331
That scene was like a one-man play Jamie Foxx
could perform on Broadway.

00:02:04.331 --> 00:02:06.829
It was one of my favorite non-action scenes.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:09.110
Just him being crazy talking to himself.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:13.630
I really did like Jamie Foxx’s Max Dillon
character better than Electro.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.260
I don’t think we’ll see him again.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.180
The Electro persona has basically taken over
by the end of the movie.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.690
But let’s talk about Dane Dehaan.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.569
Just like Jamie Foxx I really like the Harry
Osborn character before he became Green Goblin.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:30.120
A lot of you may be seeing Dane Dehaan for
the first time.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.040
We really didn’t get as much time with him
pre-transformation as we did with Jamie Foxx’s

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.590
character but my favorite Harry scene was
the board room.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.760
Everyone in this room now works for Felicia.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.260
I feel like enough time has passed that less
people thought of Jame’s Franco’s college

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.260
dropout Harry Osborn.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.260
I totally enjoyed that Harry way way back.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:50.680
But I think Dane Dehaan’s twist on the character
is a lot more interesting.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.380
He does have the benefit of being a genius
this time around.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.310
I’m not entirely sure why Norman Osborn
said he was wasting his potential.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.250
That probably had something to do with him
traveling around the world dating supermodels

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.250
after school.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:06.300
But my only big disappointment was that the
Oscorp executive became a fourth villain.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.870
I don’t know about you guys, but I felt
like it would have been a lot more fun to

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.640
see an evil dark knight version of Harry Osborn.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.680
Like the diametric opposite to Christian Bale’s
Batman.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:20.800
In that scenario he would seize control of
the company and just use it to fund his private

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.129
war against the superheroes of all the sequels
and spinoffs.

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:23.129
They weren’t really clear about what his
status and wealth are after the movie.

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:25.900
He got fired from Oscorp by the board, but
I think he still owns the company.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.940
So he’s still super rich, they just try
to lock him out of the building.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.400
I don’t know how the sequels will treat
that, because at the end he’s locked up

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.400
in Ravencroft.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.010
As for the main characters I always love Emma
Stone and given that they kind of spoiled

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:43.060
her fate in the trailer there really weren’t
any surprises from her character.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.590
I do like that her Gwen Stacy got to be a
critical part of the solution.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:52.260
But I still feel like she was wasted like
a lot of great actors get buried under these

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.459
giant movies.

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:56.239
Just like Scarlett Johansson in Avengers.

00:03:56.239 --> 00:04:02.400
I feel like Winter Soldier was a good example
of a big comic book movie that gave an equal

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.769
role to the female lead.

00:04:03.769 --> 00:04:06.129
So I feel like Sony could learn a lot from
from that.

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:09.800
We did see Felicia Hardy and even though she
was almost not even in the movie at all.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.069
I’m expecting her to get an expanded Black
Cat role in the sequels.

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:17.779
In case you don’t remember, for a couple
months Shailene Woodley was playing Mary Jane

00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:18.779
Watson.

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:22.469
They shot scenes with her and everything,
but ended up cutting her out of the movie.

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:25.689
Now that we’ve all seen it it’s easy to
understand why.

00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:29.979
The story is just trying to do so many things
I’m glad they didn’t include more characters.

00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:33.090
It would have been Spider-Man 3 all over again.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.090
So let’s talk about the story.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.839
There were a few things I really liked and
just a few things I had a big issue with.

00:04:37.839 --> 00:04:41.780
So right off the bat going into movies like
this I try to remind myself that they’re

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.199
not made for me.

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:46.150
Remember the little kid that put the spider-man
pajamas on at the end of the movie.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.270
That’s who this movie was made for.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.780
It was made for little kids.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.830
If you watch it with that in mind.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.889
I feel like you’ll enjoy yourself a lot
more.

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:55.270
Don’t expect this to be the Dark Knight
or anything.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:01.289
I love that they wanted to create a Spider
Movie Universe and I feel like Ravencroft

00:05:01.289 --> 00:05:05.789
in addition to Oscorp Special Projects did
that.

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:08.580
We even know who the Six Characters are going
to be in Sinister Six.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:13.710
I feel like those were the whole movie, you
could have called it Amazing Spider-Man 2,

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.899
Rise of The Sinister Six.

00:05:14.899 --> 00:05:16.309
And nothing would have changed.

00:05:16.309 --> 00:05:18.349
I am looking forward to the spinoffs.

00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:22.210
But remember, those movies are also going
to be written for little kids in Spider-Man

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.259
pajamas.

00:05:23.259 --> 00:05:28.011
The only issue I had with the story was the
amount of time the devoted to Spider-Man helping

00:05:28.011 --> 00:05:29.180
non-essential characters.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.119
Like the whole scene with him helping the
little kid with the windmill.

00:05:32.119 --> 00:05:35.349
That scene was there because this is a movie
for little kids.

00:05:35.349 --> 00:05:39.039
But the only other things that I felt were
tired were the jokes.

00:05:39.039 --> 00:05:42.369
I feel like trying to do silly Spider-Man
humor was Sam Raimi’s thing.

00:05:42.369 --> 00:05:45.589
And he is a master at that kind of humor.

00:05:45.589 --> 00:05:48.349
Because that was something so many people
responded to from the original trilogy, I

00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:51.930
felt like the producers were really quick
to try and force that into the Andrew Garfield

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:52.930
reboot.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.370
But I’m just not a big fan of silly Andrew
Garfield.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.759
I think he does a lot better when he’s doing
drama.

00:05:57.759 --> 00:06:01.580
And just to talk about the action and camera
work.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:05.529
I did like the creative improvements they
made to those first-person scenes.

00:06:05.529 --> 00:06:09.770
Like the opening of the movie where you’re
seeing Spider-Man’s point of view.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:13.870
The action scenes were good, but again Andrew
Garfield is a dramatic actor.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.099
Not an action hero.

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:17.210
He’s not Chris Hemsworth.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:21.029
And he doesn’t quite have the balance of
ridiculousness and sincerity that Robert Downey

00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:22.029
Jr has, yet.

00:06:22.029 --> 00:06:23.499
He’ll get there eventually.

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:27.590
He’s a great actor, so I’m interested
to see what the sequels look like.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.740
But now it’s your turn.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.509
Let me know what you thought of the movie?

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:32.930
Did you like the way they set up the spinoffs
and sequels?

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:38.669
And do you think they can create a Spider-Verse
without things getting too ridiculous?

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:45.139
Right now they’ve already confirmed Spider-Man
3 and 4 along with Sinister Six.

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:47.710
The next Spider Verse movie will be that third
sequel.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.789
They’re supposed to start production on
Sinister Six early in 2015, so that might

00:06:51.789 --> 00:06:54.780
not be out until late 2016 or spring 2017.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.399
There is a Venom movie happening too, but
that’s not supposed to appear until around

00:06:58.399 --> 00:07:00.369
Spider-Man 4.

00:07:00.369 --> 00:07:06.759
Let’s talk about the Sinister Six lineup
and that X-Men Post Credits scene though.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:10.629
In case you missed it, during the credits
of the movie when that song is playing they

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:15.369
show all that Oscorp Tech from Secret Projects,
like the Doctor Octopus harness and the Green

00:07:15.369 --> 00:07:16.369
Goblin Glider.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.789
That’s basically who the lineup is.

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:31.330
It’s Green Goblin, Doctor Octopus, Rhino,
Vulture, Kraven the Hunter and Mysterio, that

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.439
last one could be the Chameleon.

00:07:33.439 --> 00:07:35.459
But I think Mysterio would be more fun.

00:07:35.459 --> 00:07:38.919
Based on that Ravencroft scene it looks like
they’ll just use willing test subjects that

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:41.919
are in prison or just total dirtbags looking
for easy power.

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:46.080
They’ll probably stick with the original
comic book characters for each of those personas.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.439
I’m choosing to remain optimistic about
it.

00:07:49.439 --> 00:07:54.559
They cast great actors in this movie, but
a lot of it will depend on the script.

00:07:54.559 --> 00:07:56.369
Which we won’t see for a long time.

00:07:56.369 --> 00:08:02.089
Let me know what you’re thoughts are on
the Sinister Six and Venom movies that are

00:08:02.089 --> 00:08:03.089
coming.

00:08:03.089 --> 00:08:04.539
If you were confused about the X-Men Scene
at the end.

00:08:04.539 --> 00:08:08.589
Here’s what’s going on and why a Fox Movie
was part of a Sony Movie.

00:08:08.589 --> 00:08:10.209
Because those are two separate universes.

00:08:10.209 --> 00:08:14.199
Spider-Man has nothing to do with X-Men on
a story level.

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:16.749
It’s all because of the director Marc Webb.

00:08:16.749 --> 00:08:20.849
He had a contract that was still in force
at Fox when Sony hired him to Direct Amazing

00:08:20.849 --> 00:08:22.199
Spider-Man 2.

00:08:22.199 --> 00:08:27.879
Fox agreed to let him out of his contract
if Sony would promote Days of Future Past.

00:08:27.879 --> 00:08:30.840
Because Sony didn’t have a post-credits
scene for any of their spinoffs ready it just

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.900
worked out that with Days of Future Past coming
soon, they opted to use that scene to fulfill

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.900
their agreement and make fans happy.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.640
A lot of people feel like if you go to a big
comic book movie like this and you DON’T

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.640
get a post-credits scene.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.640
You’ve been cheated out of some money.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:42.640
So Sony was really happy to have something
to show, even if it wasn’t their own movie.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.130
The X-Men scene didn’t really have any relevant
plot info or spoilery stuff.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.899
It just establishes that Mystique is operating
on her own.

00:08:46.899 --> 00:08:51.329
In all the scenes we’ve had so far Magneto
and Professor X are on their own without teams.

00:08:51.329 --> 00:08:53.500
So this just helped set that up a little more.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.339
Let me know whether you liked it or just thought
it was out of place.

00:08:57.339 --> 00:09:01.612
So in related news, lots of stuff happening
in the next week.

00:09:01.612 --> 00:09:03.500
I’m doing a special Godzilla Week with Nerdist
Channel because that movie is coming out in

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.500
two weeks.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.500
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:12.500
Most of it will be fun bonus videos and my
review will post after the movie is out.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:16.440
Right now click here for my breakdown of Star
Wars Episode 7 and click here to learn more

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:17.750
about the Justice League movie.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.610
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:20.140
High Fives!

